{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, סָרַךְ","hw":"סָרַךְ","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סָרַךְ</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m. chief, overseer (</strong>𝔗 id. (= BH <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁטֵר</span>); etym. dub.; prob. with Bev Dn Dr Dn Andr<sup>M 75</sup>*, loan-word from. Pers. <em>sār</em> (and *<em>sarak</em>?), <em>head, chief</em><strong>)</strong>;—pl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָֽרְכִין</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:3\" href=\"/Daniel.6.3\">Dn 6:3</a>, emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָֽרְכַיָּא</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:4\" href=\"/Daniel.6.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:5\" href=\"/Daniel.6.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:7\" href=\"/Daniel.6.7\">7</a>, cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָֽרְכֵי</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:8\" href=\"/Daniel.6.8\">8</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, סְתַר","prev":"BDB Aramaic, סַרְבָּל"}